From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 08:11:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: mfd: cirrus,madera: Reference the SPI peripheral
 properties

Madera codecs sit on SPI as often as on I2C, but the schema does not pull
in the SPI peripheral properties, so a codec node on SPI fails validation
as soon as it carries spi-max-frequency or a controller specific child
such as the controller-data node of the Samsung SPI controller.

Reference spi-peripheral-props.yaml the way the Arizona binding already
does.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/cirrus,madera.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/cirrus,madera.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/cirrus,madera.yaml
index 68c75a517c9..da470349945 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/cirrus,madera.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/cirrus,madera.yaml
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@ description: |
     bindings/sound/cirrus,madera.yaml
 
 allOf:
+  - $ref: /schemas/spi/spi-peripheral-props.yaml
   - $ref: /schemas/pinctrl/cirrus,madera.yaml#
   - $ref: /schemas/regulator/wlf,arizona.yaml#
   - $ref: /schemas/sound/cirrus,madera.yaml#
